Role: Workday Adaptive planning Consultant
Exp: 4 to 10 years
Locations: Bang/Hyd/Chennai/Pune/Gurugram
Mode of work: Hybrid
Certifications: Workday Certified (Mandatory)

Responsibilities:
Proficient in overseeing a support ticketing queue with multiple open items, demonstrating strong written and oral communication skills;
Capable of leading client status meetings and extracting relevant metrics;
Handles client relationships, confirming effective communication;
Offers functional and/or technical subject matter expertise;
Directs process redesign efforts;
Leads technical and test teams for the implementation of functionality;
Provides recommendations to change activities to confirm business adoption and provides effective user training;
Manages the complete project lifecycle to confirm timely project delivery;
Meets with stakeholders throughout the organization to confirm a comprehensive set of requirements, aligned to business objectives, gaining a complete understanding of current and future state business processes;
Provides in-depth knowledge of the Workday application and evaluates the customers processes against the standard Workday functionality;
Demonstrates experience in use of Workday in a support/AMS environment;
Documents the business requirements which express what actions a solution should take and what outcome is expected;
Is responsible for fixes and enhancements to the application to achieve the customer’s business requirements;
Has industry experience and understands challenges and risks when providing professional services and supporting vertical applications and localizations;
Demonstrated ability to:
Analyze and understand business problems;
Model data and processes;
Conduct workshops and training sessions;
Plan and carry out system and user acceptance testing
Familiar with and experienced in:
Core application functionality;
Implementation Methodology;
Application technology stack;
ITIL process knowledge/understanding is highly preferred;
Active Workday Adaptive Planning/Adaptive Insights certification;
2+ years of experience and working knowledge with Planning Budgeting Forecasting and Management Reporting in functional roles;
Experience in multiple full lifecycle EPM projects with deep understanding and expertise in designing and implementing complex models like:
Financial Planning, e.g., Revenue Planning, Expense Planning, Projects Planning, Capital Planning, Balance Sheet and Cash Flow Planning;
Workforce Planning, e.g., Headcount/FTE and Compensation Planning, Resource Supply and Demand Planning;
Operational Planning, e.g., Sales Planning;
Ability to work on multiple projects;
Subject Matter Expertise on Budgeting Planning and Forecasting while identifying opportunities for automation and process improvements;
Ability to work with the client and drive design sessions and help customers resolve issues requiring in depth expertise;
Ability to help customers resolve functional issues requiring in depth expertise in the Adaptive solution;
Experience in creating reports utilizing advanced Excel skills and dashboards;
Analyze Workday release updates to understand impacts of feature changes, in relation to clients existing configuration;
Good to have Workday Finance/HCM/Integration certification; and;,
Functional experience and knowledge of Workday Finance/Accounting, reporting/consolidation is an advantage.

